WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.300
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.667
-Oh, my God.
-I'm very happy you're here.

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:04.901
-Me too.
-Yeah.

00:00:04.901 --> 00:00:06.767
-Yeah!
-I -- You know, I --

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:09.534
I'm so excited that you're here,
because I will tell you this.

00:00:09.534 --> 00:00:12.801
I held you as a baby.
-You -- You held me?

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:14.167
-Yeah, I held you.
-As a baby?

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:15.534
-As a baby,
I held you like this.

00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:16.901
-Crazy!

00:00:16.901 --> 00:00:19.334
-I met you with your parents --
Uma Thurman, Ethan Hawke.

00:00:19.334 --> 00:00:21.167
-Yeah, those are them.
-Yeah, and I --

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:22.634
And I held you --

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:24.868
I think it was in Rhinebeck
at someone's house,

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:26.067
and I was holding you.

00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:27.567
I think my mother
even held you, as well.

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:29.000
-Wow. See?
That's just so crazy.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.934
It's like -- I feel like
most people come here

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:33.801
on the first time,
and they get to, like,
tell you their life story.

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:35.934
-I raised you.
-Yeah.

00:00:35.934 --> 00:00:37.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:39.000
You raised me, yeah.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.000
[ Overlapping dialogue ]

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.634
-Second time we're meeting.
"Tell me about your life." Yeah.

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:45.801
But I do remember your par--
You were reading "Ferdinand."

00:00:45.801 --> 00:00:48.234
-"Ferdinand the Bull."
-Was the book you were reading.

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:49.968
-I love that book.
-And I go,

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:52.634
"Oh, I don't know that book,"
and your parents were like --

00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:54.734
Your mom was like,
"You don't know 'Ferdinand'?"

00:00:54.734 --> 00:00:57.367
-I mean, it's a classic.
-I know, but I was 20-something.

00:00:57.367 --> 00:00:59.200
I didn't read kids' books.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.501
-That's not what you read
on your day-to-day...?

00:01:01.501 --> 00:01:04.000
-No, I was reading Judy Blume
at the time.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.501
But I was like, "Okay."
And they were so nice.

00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:09.100
And I was like,
"What a cute baby."

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:12.701
And then just to watch your
career just rise right now.

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:14.400
It's just awesome.
Congratulations on everything.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.033
I'm so proud of you.
-Aww. Thank you so much.

00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:17.701
-You put the work in, bud.
-Thank you so much.

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:20.000
I mean, I don't know about that.
-Yeah, you did.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.367
-But, um, no, I mean,
it's -- it's so awesome.

00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:25.434
I was -- I called my mom
to ask for advice today

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:27.300
about coming in to talk to you.
-Yeah.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.701
-Because that's what I do.
I get to ask for advice.

00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:31.467
It's a big luxury of mine.
-Yeah.

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:33.534
-And we just got into
talking about, um,

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:35.801
like the Supreme Court ruling...
-Yeah.

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:40.334
-...and this essay
that my mom wrote, like,

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:42.133
a couple months ago
when they were putting these

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:43.601
further restrictions
on abortion access,

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:45.234
and it was sort of
preceding this whole thing.

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:48.000
And my mom wrote this really
beautiful essay about,

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.834
uh, her abortion that she got
when she was really young

00:01:50.834 --> 00:01:52.734
and about how
if she hadn't have had it,

00:01:52.734 --> 00:01:55.100
she wouldn't have become
the person that she'd become

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.767
and I wouldn't exist and how
both of my parents' lives

00:01:57.767 --> 00:02:00.834
would've been totally derailed
if she hadn't had access to safe

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:03.901
and legal healthcare --
fundamental healthcare.

00:02:03.901 --> 00:02:06.834
And I -- Of course,
like, wealthy people

00:02:06.834 --> 00:02:08.868
will always be able
to get abortions,

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:12.601
but so many people, because
of this ruling this, like, week

00:02:12.601 --> 00:02:15.968
will not only not be able
to pursue their dreams,

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:19.934
but actually lose their lives
and be unsafe, and, um --

00:02:19.934 --> 00:02:22.300
I just wanted to say that,
like, you know,

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.534
[Bleep] the Supreme Court.
-Yeah, okay, yeah.

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:27.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:27.067 --> 00:02:28.501
♪♪

00:02:28.501 --> 00:02:29.767
You can absolutely say that.

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:31.234
-Yeah, but we're going
to keep fighting this.

00:02:31.234 --> 00:02:32.534
I can say
"[Bleep] the Supreme Court"?

00:02:32.534 --> 00:02:34.334
-Yeah.
-[Bleep] the Supreme Court.

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:35.801
Yeah. Rock on.

00:02:35.801 --> 00:02:39.400
And we're gonna keep --
But we're gonna keep fighting.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.434
And we're gonna win
like our grandmothers did.

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:43.133
So I think that's good.

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:45.067
-Yeah. I'm happy
you said that message.

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:46.767
I appreciate you.
Thank you for saying that.

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:48.167
Thank you for saying
that message.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.167
Thank you.
-Thank you.

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:50.667
-I wanted to talk about --

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:52.334
I know your parents
are very proud of you.

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:54.067
-I hope so.
-Every time they're on the show,

00:02:54.067 --> 00:02:56.834
they talk about you.
-You always bring me up.
They're annoyed about it.

00:02:56.834 --> 00:02:58.434
They're like,
"I want to talk about me."

00:02:58.434 --> 00:02:59.968
-No, they don't. No.

00:02:59.968 --> 00:03:03.300
But I thought it was funny.
I looked at your Instagram bio.

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:06.000
This is @maya-hawke.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.534
And under here it says
"Tony Hawk's daughter."

00:03:08.534 --> 00:03:11.767
So your dad
must really love that.

00:03:11.767 --> 00:03:13.834
-I don't know why it's funny,
but it makes me laugh.

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:15.501
-No, it made me laugh, too.
I got it.

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:18.167
'Cause you're not
Tony Hawk's daughter.

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:19.567
-No. I know!

00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:22.601
-But you're a great actor,
and I talked to your --

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:24.367
I think it was your dad
or your mom

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:26.901
last time they were on,
and I was talking about
how proud they were.

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:28.601
It was your dad.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:30.901
-Your dad saw you perform.
-Oh.

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:32.334
Oh, as a backup singer
for my brother?

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:33.400
-Yes.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:34.534
-Yeah, that was
his favorite moment.

00:03:34.534 --> 00:03:35.734
-He got weepy. He got weepy.

00:03:35.734 --> 00:03:37.901
And he goes, "I'm just
so proud of my kids."

00:03:37.901 --> 00:03:39.834
-I think he likes seeing
my ego settle in, you know?

00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:41.767
Stand behind my brothers
a little bit.

00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:45.767
-Exactly. But you have a song
that's released right now

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:46.968
out at midnight, tonight.

00:03:46.968 --> 00:03:48.367
-Yeah!
-Congratulations. It's out.

00:03:48.367 --> 00:03:50.767
-Thank you.
-You can --

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:53.200
Now, I'm gonna -- Hopefully --

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:54.934
"Thérèse" I think
is how it's pronounced.

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:58.734
-Yeah.
-But it's spelled T-H-E-R-E-S-E.

00:03:58.734 --> 00:04:01.200
-Yeah, it has two little guys
on it, too, little French guys.

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.501
-Yes. "Thérèse."
-"Thérèse."

00:04:03.501 --> 00:04:04.667
-"Thérèse."
-Yeah.

00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:06.400
-And what does --
What does that mean?

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.667
-It's the name of a --
There's a painting at the Met,

00:04:08.667 --> 00:04:10.100
and it's called
"Thérèse Dreaming."

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.901
And it's the name
of the girl in the painting,

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:14.067
and it's a song about
the girl in the painting

00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:17.100
who, in my head, is me.
So, yeah.

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.968
-I love that you made it.
You were explaining it to me.

00:04:19.968 --> 00:04:22.567
You were like, "Well, I'm lucky
I'm acting, which is awesome."

00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:25.534
But when you're acting, there's
also a lot of time that you're

00:04:25.534 --> 00:04:27.801
just kind of waiting around for
lights or something to happen.

00:04:27.801 --> 00:04:29.701
You're like, "I'm not gonna
waste any time, man.

00:04:29.701 --> 00:04:31.067
I'm Maya Hawke.
I'm ready to go."

00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:32.968
-Where's a napkin?
Where's the back of my sides?

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:34.534
-"Let's write something."

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:35.834
And you have an album...

00:04:35.834 --> 00:04:37.067
-Yeah.
--...coming out. I'm gonna --

00:04:37.067 --> 00:04:38.567
-I've never seen that.

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:40.167
-I know I'm about to show you
for the first time.

00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:41.601
This is your real --
This is your vinyl.

00:04:41.601 --> 00:04:43.968
-We got it made especially
for you -- an early release.

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:45.701
Oh, it's so cool!
It's see-through?!

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:47.667
-Oh, yeah.
-Oh! Look at that.

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:49.133
I can see you through it.

00:04:49.133 --> 00:04:51.534
-Is that rad?
Is that the coolest?

00:04:51.534 --> 00:04:53.000
-Aah! That's so rad!
-"Moss."

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.100
"Moss" is the name of the album.
-Be careful. I'm --

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.601
-Yeah, be careful.
Yeah, of course.

00:04:56.601 --> 00:04:58.834
-But that's the first time
I've -- That's the first one.

00:04:58.834 --> 00:05:00.133
We got it pressed for you.

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.667
-You -- You -- This is it.
-Yeah.

00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:03.100
-Are you excited?
-Yeah!

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:05.033
-Yeah, alright, good.
When does this come out?

00:05:05.033 --> 00:05:06.767
Do we know?
-Uh, it comes out in September.

00:05:06.767 --> 00:05:08.100
-September.

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.701
-Yeah, back-to-school record
is kind of the premise.

00:05:09.701 --> 00:05:12.000
-It's a back-to-school record.
It's called "Moss."

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:14.868
It's Maya Hawke.

00:05:14.868 --> 00:05:17.567
I want to talk to you
about "Stranger Things."

00:05:17.567 --> 00:05:19.701
-That's what I want
to talk about.

00:05:19.701 --> 00:05:21.467
-It's the biggest show
in the world.

00:05:21.467 --> 00:05:24.767
-Yeah. It's big.
-It's giant. It is.

00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:27.267
It's number one on Netflix in
over 80 countries, by the way.

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:28.567
-That's crazy.

00:05:28.567 --> 00:05:30.067
-Yeah, isn't that wild?
-Yeah.

00:05:30.067 --> 00:05:31.300
-It's the biggest thing ever.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.033
You're fantastic in it.
-Thank you!

00:05:33.033 --> 00:05:35.567
-Volume 2 comes out July 1st.

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:36.734
-Yeah.
-This Friday.

00:05:36.734 --> 00:05:38.133
-Yeah!
-Yeah, exactly.

00:05:38.133 --> 00:05:41.067
Now, what can you say
about these episodes?

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:42.567
Anything -- No spoilers, right?

00:05:42.567 --> 00:05:45.567
-Well, the thing is, we filmed
them a long time ago now.

00:05:45.567 --> 00:05:47.801
It takes a long time to --
put it together.

00:05:47.801 --> 00:05:49.601
-Sure.
-And so, I know --

00:05:49.601 --> 00:05:51.534
I know that I know what happens.
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:51.534 --> 00:05:54.100
-But can I tell --
I don't remember exactly.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:56.534
[ Laughter ]
I -- I haven't seen them yet.

00:05:56.534 --> 00:05:58.734
And I don't remember exactly,
but that's why I'm excited

00:05:58.734 --> 00:06:01.601
'cause I'm so excited
to just see how it all wraps up.

00:06:01.601 --> 00:06:03.767
-Those guys are pretty amazing,
those Duffer brothers.

00:06:03.767 --> 00:06:05.567
-They're so smart.
They're such good writers.

00:06:05.567 --> 00:06:06.834
I don't know if you've noticed

00:06:06.834 --> 00:06:08.734
that I'm talking like
Phoebe Buffay on Adderall.

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:10.701
Like, I do this really
fast-talking thing.

00:06:10.701 --> 00:06:12.501
But they noticed
when I come on set --

00:06:12.501 --> 00:06:14.501
I don't do it all the time
with my friends,

00:06:14.501 --> 00:06:16.400
but when I get nervous,
it, like, all --

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:19.133
And so they noticed that I do
that 'cause I was nervous on set

00:06:19.133 --> 00:06:21.634
and then they wrote me
so much dialogue this season.

00:06:21.634 --> 00:06:24.267
I know if you noticed,
but I have these giant page-long

00:06:24.267 --> 00:06:26.100
monologues, and they're like,
"No, do, don't worry.

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:29.234
You'll just do it in 2 minutes.
You'll do it real fast."

00:06:29.234 --> 00:06:31.667
-But a normal actor
would read this,

00:06:31.667 --> 00:06:33.234
it'll take them 30 minutes.

00:06:33.234 --> 00:06:35.801
Maya's gonna nail this
in 2 seconds, yeah.

00:06:35.801 --> 00:06:37.868
-One breath. Brrr!
-Brrr! Yeah.

00:06:37.868 --> 00:06:40.901
You're so fun and so good.
I love your character.

00:06:40.901 --> 00:06:43.300
And you just --
You fit right in because --

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:46.234
Was it last season was the first
season you debuted, right?

00:06:46.234 --> 00:06:47.901
-Yeah.
-And I was like,

00:06:47.901 --> 00:06:49.934
"Oh, my gosh.
It's Maya. I love you."

00:06:49.934 --> 00:06:52.234
-"I held that baby!"
"I held that baby!"

00:06:52.234 --> 00:06:55.200
-"I held that baby!"
-"That's my girl." Yeah.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.334
-She likes "Ferdinand the Bull"!

00:06:57.334 --> 00:06:59.701
-Yes! Of course!
And you just nailed it.

00:06:59.701 --> 00:07:01.501
Alright.
So get ready. July 1st.

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:04.868
This is volume 2, season 4.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:04.868 --> 00:07:08.067
Here's Maya Hawke in season 4 of
"Stranger Things." Take a look.

00:07:08.067 --> 00:07:09.534
♪♪

00:07:09.534 --> 00:07:10.901
-And then Vickie laughed.

00:07:10.901 --> 00:07:12.567
And it wasn't like a cheap
fake laugh, either.

00:07:12.567 --> 00:07:15.300
It was like --
It was a real, genuine laugh.

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:16.567
-Of course she laughed, Robin.

00:07:16.567 --> 00:07:17.801
It's my Muppet joke.
It's hilarious.

00:07:17.801 --> 00:07:20.234
-My point is
that Vickie laughed

00:07:20.234 --> 00:07:22.767
and everything was just,
like -- it was perfect.

00:07:22.767 --> 00:07:24.901
-But?
-But I'm having this problem,

00:07:24.901 --> 00:07:27.234
where it's like
I should stop talking.

00:07:27.234 --> 00:07:28.968
I have said everything
I need to say.

00:07:28.968 --> 00:07:31.067
But then I guess I get nervous,
and the words,

00:07:31.067 --> 00:07:32.934
they just --
they keep spilling out.

00:07:32.934 --> 00:07:35.067
And it's like my -- my brain
is moving faster than my mouth,

00:07:35.067 --> 00:07:37.367
or -- or rather m-my mouth
is moving faster than my brain,

00:07:37.367 --> 00:07:39.267
and it's like I'm digging
this hole for myself,

00:07:39.267 --> 00:07:40.968
and I want to stop digging
and I'm trying to stop digging,

00:07:40.968 --> 00:07:44.334
but I can't -- and I'm doing it
right now, aren't I?

00:07:44.334 --> 00:07:46.400
-Yeah, you are.
-[ Sighs ]

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:49.167
-Yeah, that's how you do it.

00:07:49.167 --> 00:07:50.834
Maya Hawke, everybody!

00:07:50.834 --> 00:07:53.100
Season 4, volume 2
of "Stranger Things"

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:55.434
premiers July 1st on Netflix.

00:07:55.434 --> 00:07:59.434
And Maya's new album, "Moss,"
is out September 23rd!

00:07:59.434 --> 00:08:01.133
You can preorder it now.

